  "title": "Reading 2.2: Grounding and “Insufficient Evidence”",
  "text": "Grounding: Instructing and checking a model so its answer comes from the documents or data you provide, and says “insufficient evidence” when they can't support an answer. Why it matters: The most valuable sentence an AI system can produce in a business is sometimes “the evidence doesn't say”.\nWhen the right answer is “I can't tell”. Suppose you have a table of late deliveries by region and someone asks which carrier caused the most delays. The table has no carrier column. Any carrier named in the answer is invented, however confident it sounds. The grounded answer is that the evidence is insufficient, plus what data would settle it.\nPrompt controls that make this happen. Use only the supplied table or document. If the question can't be answered from it, say “insufficient evidence”. Name the source for every figure. Separate what the evidence shows from any assumption."
