  "text": "Double counting: Counting the same records more than once, often because an export includes subtotal or Grand Total rows that are then summed with the detail rows. Why it matters: Every downstream figure inherits the error, and nothing on screen tells you.\nTwo exports, two answers. Two people export total sales for a state from the same Tableau crosstab. One gets the right total; the other gets exactly double. The second export kept the yearly subtotals and the Grand Total row, then summed the whole column.\nThe ten-second check. Compare the row count with the order count you expect. Compare one control total, such as total sales, with SUM(Sales) in Tableau. If either is off, find out why before you chart anything."
