  "text": "Z-pattern layout: Most important number top-left, the richest interaction top-right, detail below. If a stakeholder reads only the top row, they still get the headline. Why it matters: A VP gives a dashboard about five seconds before deciding whether to keep looking.\nWireframe first. Sketch the screen before opening Tableau: title bar naming the business and the state, two KPI cards top-left, a map top-right that filters the rest, segments, forecast and what-if along the bottom, and one narrow filter column.\nColor means one thing. Pick a meaning for each color and never break it: for example orange for current year, grey for prior year, red for loss, green for profit. No color for decoration.\nThe five-second test. Show the dashboard to someone for five seconds, then ask what it said. If they can't answer, the top row isn't doing its job."
